rules.message:
The `middleware.ts` convention is deprecated in Next.js 16 in favor of `proxy.ts`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (middleware.ts)
export function middleware(request: Request) {
  return NextResponse.next();
}

// ✅ AFTER (proxy.ts)
export default function proxy(request: Request) {
  return NextResponse.next();
}
```
</details>

