rules.message:
`revalidateTag` has changed in Next.js 16. Use `updateTag()` for instant cache purging.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
import { revalidateTag } from 'next/cache';
revalidateTag('posts');

// ✅ AFTER
import { updateTag } from 'next/cache';
updateTag('posts');
```
</details>

`serverRuntimeConfig` and `publicRuntimeConfig` have been removed in Next.js 16.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (next.config.js)
module.exports = {
  serverRuntimeConfig: { secretKey: process.env.SECRET }
};

// ✅ AFTER
// Access environment variables directly
const secretKey = process.env.SECRET;
```
</details>

Custom `webpack` configuration in `next.config.js` is ignored under Turbopack in Next.js 16.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (next.config.js)
module.exports = {
  webpack: (config) => { return config; }
};

// ✅ AFTER
module.exports = {
  turbopack: { rules: { /* Turbopack loader rules */ } }
};
```
</details>

`export const runtime = 'edge'` in middleware is deprecated in Next.js 16.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
export const runtime = 'edge';
export function middleware(req) {}

// ✅ AFTER
// Run on Node.js runtime by default
export default function proxy(req) {}
```
</details>

`getInitialProps` is deprecated in Next.js 16 in favor of App Router.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
Page.getInitialProps = async (ctx) => { return { data: 123 }; };

// ✅ AFTER (App Router page.tsx)
export default async function Page() {
  const data = await fetchData();
  return <div>{data}</div>;
}
```
</details>

